// SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause
//
// IronSide TE two-phase provisioning, PHASE 2: PRoT Provisioning -> Secured.
// Closes the non-secure AP. One operation, on the NON-SECURE firmware.
//
// Step 3 of 4, referencing no files.
//
//   1. (no erase -- ERASEPROTECT is engaged by now, and the images this phase
//      runs on top of are the point)
//   2. program production_two_phase_2.hex   -- RAM only; this bundle has no
//      NVM/UICR sections at all, it IS the non-secure provisioning firmware and
//      its one-operation batch. (A PRoT-Provisioning bundle carrying an App,
//      without UICR.OTP data, or a DFU image would have an NVM half too;
//      program that as well.)
//   3. JLinkExe -nogui 1 -SelectEmuBySN <SN> -CommandFile two_phase_2.jlink \
//              -Log results/two_phase_2.log
//   4. check_prov_result.py --bundle production_two_phase_2.hex \
//              --result results/result.bin
//
// Run two_phase_1.jlink first, and let the part BOOT -- this script redirects the
// live non-secure image UROT handed off to, so that handover must have happened.
//
// !! THE ORDER HERE IS THE OPPOSITE OF THE SECURE PHASES, and it is the awkward
// !! part of this flow. Those must not boot between programming and the script;
// !! this one MUST have booted -- and the boot puts IronSide DFU in the very RAM
// !! the programmed firmware occupies, overwriting it. So step 2 has to happen
// !! AFTER the part has booted, not before: boot it, then program, then run this.
// !! Which means for this phase alone the programmer must be able to write RAM
// !! while an image is running, and must not reset when it is done.
//
// !! The live core may be running Thread mode on PSP_NS rather than MSP_NS
// !! (CONTROL_NS.SPSEL is whatever the resident image left it at, unlike the
// !! secure phases' post-reset core, which starts SPSEL=0). Register 13
// !! resolves to whichever bank is selected, and only that bank's write takes
// !! effect -- so both PSP_NS and MSP_NS are set below to the same value,
// !! regardless of which one the redirect will actually use.
//
// !! The resident image's stack limits also stay set. Both MSPLIM_NS and
// !! PSPLIM_NS are cleared below, since a stack pointer below either limit
// !! faults the firmware's first push.
//
// The bundle comes from:
//   ironside_bundle.py build-production-hex <bundle> -o <dir>
//
// which writes this phase's hex alongside two_phase_1's and the single-phase hex.

EoE 1
SelectInterface SWD
Speed 4000
// The secure AP is burned by now, so this attaches non-secure.
Device Cortex-M33
Connect

// --- Halt the LIVE non-secure image. No reset: a Cortex-M33 always resets into
// --- secure state, so a reset-and-halt can only ever catch the secure boot
// --- entry, never the non-secure one. A reset would also boot IronSide DFU over
// --- the firmware programmed in step 2.
//
// !! NO GUARD. The Python driver checks the halted PC lands in non-secure flash
// !! and retries up to five times, because a single halt can land inside a
// !! secure NSC excursion -- from which this redirect would not take. Commander
// !! cannot branch on the read, so the PC is logged and the redirect proceeds
// !! regardless. This is the weakest step in the whole set.
Halt
RReg R15

// --- Clear the result header.
W4 0x20071000, 0x00000000
W4 0x20071004, 0x00000000
W4 0x20071008, 0x00000000
W4 0x2007100C, 0x00000000

// --- Redirect into the non-secure provisioning firmware, which routes
// --- set-approtect through UROT's device-management service over the secure
// --- gateway -- the secure AP being gone is the whole reason for this phase.
// ---
// --- Banked non-secure VTOR, matching the Python driver. Both non-secure stack
// --- pointer banks are set to the same value: Commander has no spelling for
// --- register index 13 (see single_phase.jlink), so there is no way to write
// --- only whichever bank CONTROL_NS.SPSEL currently selects.
W4 0xE002ED08, 0x20013000
WReg MSP_NS, 0x20032800
WReg PSP_NS, 0x20032800
WReg MSPLIM_NS, 0x00000000
WReg PSPLIM_NS, 0x00000000
SetPC 0x20012800
WReg XPSR, 0x01000000
Go

WaitHalt 10000
SaveBin results/result.bin, 0x20071000, 0x200

// --- Commit with a pin reset -> Secured.
WriteDP 2 0x02000000
WriteAP 0 0x00000004
WriteAP 0 0x00000000
qc
